  "core_message": "A bear eating a lost drug drop became a real 1985 murder mystery.",
  "mood": "curious",
  "title": "Cocaine‑Fueled Bear Rampage: The 1985 Georgia Murder Puzzle",
  "description": "In 1985, a pilot dropped a bag of cocaine in a Georgia forest and died hitting the doorframe. A black bear ate the drugs, became violent, and one hiker never came home.\n\nThe police found the bear's stomach full of cocaine. The case never got solved, but it became a legend.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"Cocaine Bear\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocaine_Bear), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImages from Wikimedia Commons:\nElizabeth Banks by Gage Skidmore.jpg (Gage Skidmore, CC BY-SA 3.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elizabeth_Banks_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg\nCocaine Bear, Kentucky for Kentucky Fun Mall (cropped).jpg (Ferrett333, CC BY-SA 4.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cocaine_Bear,_Kentucky_for_Kentucky_Fun_Mall_(cropped).jpg",
